  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The manual text only says the PIR has three pins that connect to the Raspberry Pi and gives no pin table, so the pins are assumed: VCC to 5V.1 (the PIR supply range is 4.5-20 V), GND to GND.1, and OUT to GPIO4, a general-purpose input.",
   "The PIR OUT signal is typically 3.3 V, so it is safe for the Pi's 3.3 V-only GPIO input. VCC goes to 5V, not 3V3.",
   "The wires are assumed to be female-to-female jumpers between the PIR header pins and the Pi header. The catalogue has no such type, so the generic jumper-wire is used.",
   "No breadboard is used, since the manual does not mention one."
  ]
 },
